// program-image-fkb-byte-decode.fk -- decode canonical program-image .fkb bytes.
//
// Layer 8h6 is an artifact-format decoder and witness-admission layer. It
// decodes the 8h4 byte grammar back into the encoded program-image payload and
// admits an 8h5 readback witness only when the readback bytes decode
// canonically and match the external witness/container metadata.
//
// The v5 witness decoder remains pure. The v8 path below patches one admitted
// image from a restricted evaluator's captured proof, then conditionally
// publishes it through the existing guarded rename door. It preserves the
// owning image's metadata and reports publication care through organ-health.
// Neither path executes the image or snapshots unrelated process state.
//
